eld-out task/episode split are required.\nESTIMAND: for each site r, C_r estimates the mean dimensionless one-control-transition consequence of intervening on r over the calibration episode distribution D_cal, conditional on the same h_j, l_j, denoising seed xi_j, simulator state z_j, and simulator seed eta_j; it is not an unbiased estimate of global task-success loss or of an arbitrary real-robot deployment population.\nlineage constraint: the load-bearing artifact is the paired action-to-simulator-observation counterfactual, not n1 layer-local PTQ, n2 static sensitivity allocation, n3 QuantWM latent rollout/planning, or n4 QuantWAMs joint empirical-Fisher scoring and fixed-count schedule repair.\nBLOCK 2 — NAIVE-BASELINE AUDIT (branch (i))\nThe naive version is runnable-in-principle local PTQ: compute each site's FP16-versus-low-bit local output discrepancy on open-loop calibration inputs and upgrade the top-B sites. It does not already work because it silently assumes that local discrepancy is a sufficient proxy for downstream consequence, and that premise is false in this setting: a changed action chunk changes the next observation and therefore the inputs to later coupled predictions and contact dynamics. The mechanism confronts that failure head-on with paired simulator counterfactuals; ordinary local sensitivity or one-step PTQ does not resolve the WAM-specific combination of coupled video/action denoising, action-mediated state transition, and contact-critical feedback, so this is not a textbook tool application with the structure removed.\nBLOCK 3 — design rationale\nBoth gaps share one intervention registry and one C_r object: the anchor uses it to allocate precision, while the sibling uses the same contexts to isolate whether L_r agrees with it, so no second architecture or dataset is needed. A replay-only local profile in the style of QuantWAMs was rejected because it never executes the changed action to obtain the next observation, and a full Jacobian-product or latent-rollout planner was rejected because it would add unobserved assumptions and move the branch into the excluded latent planning route. The chosen design therefore preserves the WAM's coupled future/action path, adds only a one-site causal diagnostic and matched allocation operator, and explicitly avoids the occupied ancestral nodes and the already-covered QuantWAMs mechanisms.",
